9":{"changeset":"Z:3hl>2|5l=3fz=7*1+2$im","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660826903}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1000":{"changeset":"Z:3hn>1|5l=3fz=9*1+1$p","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660827395,"pool":{"numToAttrib":{"0":["author","a.etherpad-system"],"1":["author","a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD"],"2":["heading","h3"],"3":["insertorder","first"],"4":["list","bullet1"],"5":["lmkr","1"],"6":["list","indent1"],"7":["list","indent3"],"8":["start","1"],"9":["author","a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5"],"10":["author","a.oIZ496sC0MvFJBbg"],"11":["list","indent2"],"12":["author","a.6fEK8VUdbD4cP299"],"13":["author","a.W8SlWkw9QzdnoaRT"],"14":["heading","h2"],"15":["list","indent4"],"16":["list","indent10"],"17":["list","indent9"],"18":["list","indent8"],"19":["list","indent7"],"20":["list","indent6"],"21":["author","a.v1tf3cnZGGlguTDX"]},"attribToNum":{"author,a.etherpad-system":0,"author,a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD":1,"heading,h3":2,"insertorder,first":3,"list,bullet1":4,"lmkr,1":5,"list,indent1":6,"list,indent3":7,"start,1":8,"author,a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5":9,"author,a.oIZ496sC0MvFJBbg":10,"list,indent2":11,"author,a.6fEK8VUdbD4cP299":12,"author,a.W8SlWkw9QzdnoaRT":13,"heading,h2":14,"list,indent4":15,"list,indent10":16,"list,indent9":17,"list,indent8":18,"list,indent7":19,"list,indent6":20,"author,a.v1tf3cnZGGlguTDX":21},"nextNum":22},"atext":{"text":"*Welcome for the training on Techno functional training program\nAgenda:\n  1.  Introduction\n  2.   LET  portal \n  3.   Day schedule (9 30am to 6 30pm)\n*    11 30  (20 minutes)\n* Lunch 1 30 ( 60 minute)\n*4  (20 minute)\n*\n   4. Lab guidance\n   5. Courseware\n   6. TOC\n   \n   9664670840\n   \n*   https://linuxlab.koenig-solutions.com\n*   Pa$$w0rd\n==================================================================================================\nApllication development:\n    Monolithic: \n    Microservice:\n        \n        components:\n            1)frontend ==>dotnet==>EFcore\n\n=================================\nSQL server==>DB server\n\nSSMS ==>Db client\n\nCRUD operation\n\nblameless postmortum\n\ncode===>build===>test==>deploy===>maintain\n==========================================\nAccount required for training:\n    ------------------------------------\ngithub\ndocker hub\nredhat\n==========================================\nDatabase\nUI\n\nDTO===>ORM\n=============================================\n*Day 2: 20/10/20\n\n\nhttps://github.com/Mudassir-dev0ps/dotnetSampleApp\n\nMVC\n============================================================\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\nusing OrderManagement.Models;\n \nnamespace OrderManagement.Data\n{\n    public class ApplicationDbContext : DbContext\n    {\n        public ApplicationDbContext(\n            DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options)\n            : base(options)\n        {\n        }\n \n        public DbSet<Customer> Customers { get; set; }\n \n        public DbSet<Order> Orders { get; set; }\n    }\n}\n\n\n=\ndll===> format===>published application\n=========================================\nvar builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);\n \nvar app = builder.Build();\n \napp.MapGet(\"/\", () =>\n    \"Hello! My .NET application is running.\");\n \napp.MapGet(\"/about\", () => new\n{\n    Application = \"BuildPublishDemo\",\n    Technology = \"ASP.NET Core\",\n    Status = \"Running\"\n});\n \napp.MapGet(\"/health\", () => new\n{\n    Status = \"Healthy\",\n    Time = DateTime.UtcNow\n});\n \napp.Run();\n\n============================================================================\n*Day 3: 21/10/23\n\nDay 6 – Windows Server Fundamentals\n•\nWindows Server architecture\n•\nWindows Server editions\n•\nSystem configuration\n•\nWindows Server roles\n•\nServer Manager\n•\nUsers and groups\n•\nLocal vs domain accounts\n•\nActive Directory overview\n•\nGroup concepts\n•\nUser management\n•\nHands-on user/group administration\n\n======================================================\nOS\ndependencies\nlibraries\nApp code\n===========================================\n\nIdentity management ===>Authentication=================>IAM\nAccess managennt====>Authorization\n\nAD=============>Windows\nLDAP===========>Linux\nEntra ID====>Azure\nIAM===>AWS\n============================================================\nThe participants will act as junior Windows Server administrators for a fictional company. They will configure a server, install roles, create users and groups, deploy Active Directory, and troubleshoot access and account-management issues.\n\n1 role==>UI\n1 role==powershell\n------------------------------------------\nlocal user\n2 local group\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAD\nlocal user\n2 local graoup\n------------------------------------\n===================================================================\n*Day 3 22/10/26\n*Windows Filesystem & Permissions\n•\nWindows filesystem\n•\nDrives and partitions\n•\nNTFS\n•\nFile and folder permissions\n•\nNTFS permissions\n•\nShare permissions\n•\nPermission inheritance\n•\nOwnership\n•\nAdministrative shares\n•\nDisk space troubleshooting\n=============================================\n3GB====10x3==1000\n3GiB===2x10=3072\n==========================\nFolder1==========>f1,f2===>content ===================>UI\nFolder2=========>f3,f4========>content===========>Powershell\n\n*Access:          Folder          FIles\n    Read                  \n    Write \n    Execute \n    \n    ACL====> access control list          \n    ACE   \n    \n    icacls (powershell command for ACL access)\n    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/icacls#:~:text=A%20sequence%20of%20simple%20rights,%2D%20Read%20and%20execute%20access\n    \n    \n#icacls C:\\NTFSDemo\\Finance /grant \"FinanceLab:(OI)(CI)M\"\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nhttps://rms.koenig-solutions.com/InterimFeedback.aspx?id=b2b7bbbabdb5&frm=3 (interim feedback)\n    \n    Learning principle\n    1)simp\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n","attribs":"*1*2*3*4*5*8+1*1|5+45*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+o*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+p*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+f*1*3*6*5+1*1|7+1x*a*3*6*5+1*1+f*a|1+q*a*3*6*5+1*a+b*1|2+2s*1+2*a+1*1|m+bo*1+6*9|1+1*1|6+35*1*2*3*5+1*1|p+fe*d|3+4*1|m+cq*1+a*d|2+2*1|1+25*1*2*3*5+1*1|u+b4*1+8*9|1+1*1|g+gt*1+a*d+1*1|7+5i*1*e*3*5+1*1|1+f*1*2*3*5+1*1|s+d4*1*3*6*5+1*1|b+ai*1+4*a|1+1*1|4+6w*a|1+5*a+4*1|1+j*1+a*a|a+1a*a+4|1+1"}}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1001":{"changeset":"Z:3ho>1|5l=3fz=a*1+1$l","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660828458}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1002":{"changeset":"Z:3hp>3|5l=3fz=b*1+3$e t","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660829040}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1003":{"changeset":"Z:3hs>2|5l=3fz=e*1+2$o ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660829603}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1004":{"changeset":"Z:3hu>1|5l=3fz=g*1+1$c","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660830168}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1005":{"changeset":"Z:3hv>2|5l=3fz=h*1+2$om","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660830738}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1006":{"changeset":"Z:3hx>3|5l=3fz=j*1+3$ple","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660831249}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1007":{"changeset":"Z:3i0>1|5l=3fz=m*1+1$x","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660831834}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1008":{"changeset":"Z:3i1>5|5l=3fz=n*1|1+1*1+4$\n    ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660833535}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1009":{"changeset":"Z:3i6>1|5m=3gn=4*1+1$2","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660834210}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1010":{"changeset":"Z:3i7>1|5m=3gn=5*1+1$)","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792660834978}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1011":{"changeset":"Z:3i8>2|5m=3gn=6*1+