g*1*t+q*1|1+1*1*t+q*1|1+1*1*t+h*1|2+2t*1*t+g*1|7+29*1*t+c*1|1+1*1*t+i*1|2+6*1*3*4*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*4*5+1*1|1+r*1*3*4*5+1*1|1+g*1*3*4*5+1*1|7+2e*1*t+s*1|8+2u*1*t+o*1|v+7l*1*t+14*1|2+2*1*t+8*1|4+a7*1*t+1i*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|1+1*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*8+1*1|1+1g*1*3*v*5*8+1*1|1+i*1*3*w*5*8+1*1|1+l*1*3*w*5*x+1*1|1+i*1*3*w*5*y+1*1|1+6*1*3*w*5*z+1*1|1+n*1*3*v*5*10+1*1|2+18*1*t+a*1|2+2*1*t+16*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|2+n*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*11+1*1|1+15*1*3*v*5*11+1*1|1+10*1*3*w*5*11+1*1|1+i*1*t+1*1|2+2*1*t+1c*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|a+42*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*12+1*1|1+11*1*3*v*5*12+1*1|1+y*1*3*v*5*12+1*1|1+k*1*3*v*5*12+1*1|1+d*1*3*v*5*12+1*1|1+j*1*3*w*5*12+1*1|1+u*1*3*w*5*13+1*1|1+1j*1*t+a*1|2+2*1*t+1f*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|6+3l*1*t+q*1|7+33*1*t+1a*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|8+2f*1*t+5*1|2+8*1*t+h*1|b+2e*1*t+1i*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|1+1*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*14+1*1|1+1k*1*3*v*5*14+1*1|1+1q*1*3*v*5*14+1*1|1+15*1*3*v*5*14+1*1|1+b*1*3*v*5*14+1*1|2+n*1*t+11*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|3+y*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*15+1*1|1+o*1*3*v*5*15+1*1|1+o*1*3*v*5*15+1*1|1+r*1*3*v*5*15+1*1|1+i*1*3*v*5*15+1*1|2+14*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*16+1*1|5+18*1*t+1k*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|2+16*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*17+1*1|1+19*1*3*v*5*17+1*1|1+1c*1*3*v*5*17+1*1|1+14*1*3*v*5*17+1*1|1+g*1*3*w*5*17+1*1|1+k*1*3*w*5*18+1*1|1+6*1*3*w*5*19+1*1|1+d*1*3*w*5*1a+1*1|2+k*1*t+1j*1|1+1*1*t+c*1|2+p*1*3*v*5+1*1|1+2*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1|1+z*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1|1+j*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1|1+k*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1|1+h*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1|1+11*1*3*v*5*1b+1*1+z$Part A: Dotnet  (35 Marks)\nEmployee Management System\nProblem Statement\nDevelop an ASP.NET Core MVC application using Entity Framework Core to manage employee information.\nEmployee Details\nCreate an Employee model with the following fields:\nId\nName\nDepartment\nSalary\n \nRequirements\n1. Create Database\nUse:\n* \n*Entity     Framework Core \n*SQL     Server \n*Code     First Approach\nPerform:\nShell\nAdd-Migration InitialCreate\nUpdate-Database\n \n\n2. Implement CRUD Operations\nEmployee should support:\n✅ Create Employee\n✅ View Employee List\n✅ Edit Employee\n✅ Delete Employee\n\n \nFiles They Should Create\nPlain Text\nModels\n└── Employee.cs\n \nData\n└── AppDbContext.cs\n \nControllers\n└── EmployeeController.cs\n \nViews\n└── Employee\n├── Index.cshtml\n├── Create.cshtml\n├── Edit.cshtml\n└── Delete.cshtml\n \n \nBuild the and publish it\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nPart B: Windows administration:\nWindows Server 2022 Practical Assessment\n\nScenario\nYou have been assigned as a Junior Windows Server Administrator. A new file server has been deployed and needs initial configuration, user management, storage configuration, permissions assignment, and troubleshooting.\nComplete all tasks using GUI tools only (Server Manager, Computer Management, Disk Management, Task Manager, Resource Monitor, Services Console).\n\nTask 1: Server Information and Configuration (5 Marks)\nRequirements\n* \n*Identify     the Windows Server edition installed. \n*Identify:        \n*Computer      Name  \n*IP      Address  \n*RAM  \n*CPU      Information  \n*Rename     the server to:\n<YOUR_NAME>-SRV01\nEvaluation\n\nTask 2: Roles and Server Manager (5 Marks)\nRequirements\nUsing Server Manager:\n* \n*Identify     currently installed roles. \n*Install     the following role:    \n*File      Server \n \n\nTask 3: User and Group Administration (10 Marks)\nRequirements\nCreate the following local users:\nPlain Text\n<YOUR_NAME>-finance01\n<YOUR_NAME>-finance02\n \nCreate local groups:\nFinanceUsers\nFileAdmins\nPerform:\n* \n*Add     both users to FinanceUsers. \n*Add     finance01 to FileAdmins. \n*Set     password:  \n*P@ssw0rd123 \n*Configure:        \n*Password      never expires  \n*User      must change password at next logon disabled \nEvaluation\n\nTask 4: File System and NTFS Permissions (10 Marks)\nRequirements\nCreate folder structure:\nD:\\CompanyData\nD:\\CompanyData\\<YOUR_NAME>-Finance\nD:\\CompanyData\\<YOUR_NAME>-HR\nConfigure permissions:\n<YOUR_NAME>-Finance Folder\nRemove Users group.\nGrant:\nFinanceUsers = Modify\nAdministrators = Full Control\nVerify resulting permissions.\n\nTask 5: Shared Folder Configuration (10 Marks)\nRequirements\nShare:\nD:\\CompanyData\\<YOUR_NAME>-Finance\n \nShare name:\nFinanceShare\nConfigure:\n     \nGroup\n      \nShare  Permission\n        \nFinanceUsers\n      \nChange\n        \nAdministrators\n      \nFull Control\n   \n\nTask 6: Permission Inheritance and Ownership (5 Marks)\nRequirements\n* \n*Disable     inheritance on <YOUR_NAME>-Finance folder. \n*Convert     inherited permissions into explicit permissions. \n*Change     ownership of the folder to:  \n*finance01 \n*Verify     ownership.\n\nTask 7: Storage Management (10 Marks)\nRequirements\nA new disk is attached.\nPerform:\n* \n*Bring     disk Online. \n*Initialize     as GPT. \n*Create     Simple Volume. \n*Format     NTFS. \n*Assign     drive letter:\n<YOUR_NAME>-F:\n* \n*Create     volume label:\nPlain Text\nDATA\n \n\nTask 9: Process Monitoring and Troubleshooting (5 Marks)\nRequirements\nUsing Task Manager and Resource Monitor:\n* \n*Identify     process consuming highest CPU. \n*Identify     process consuming highest memory. \n*Sort     processes by CPU utilization. \n*Record:        \n*Process      Name  \n*PID  \n*CPU      %  \n*Memory      Usage \n\nTask 10: Services Administration and Recovery (5 Marks)\nRequirements\nUsing Services Console:\n* \n*Locate     Print Spooler service. \n*Stop     service. \n*Start     service. \n*Configure:      \n*First     Failure = Restart Service \n*Identify     one dependent service.","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792831876185}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1766":{"changeset":"Z:b5y>2|gi=b15*8=1|1=2*x=1|1=z*y=1|1=j*z=1|1=k*10=1|1=h*11=1|1=11*1c=1=z*1|1+1*1*3*v*5*12+1$\n*","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833560566}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1767":{"changeset":"Z:b60>0|gp=b5y-1*1+1$=","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833561357}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1768":{"changeset":"Z:b60>g|gp=b5y=1*1+g$================","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833561917}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1769":{"changeset":"Z:b6g>k|gp=b5y=h*1+k$====================","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833562545}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1770":{"changeset":"Z:b70>f|gp=b5y=11*1+f$===============","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833563114}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1771":{"changeset":"Z:b7f>1|gp=b5y=1g*1|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833563700}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1772":{"changeset":"Z:b7g>1d|gq=b7f*1+1d$https://tmpfiles.org/wkA6UYOHRw6K/evaluation.docx","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833564365}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1773":{"changeset":"Z:b8t<1d|gq=b7f-1d$","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833752784}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1774":{"changeset":"Z:b7g>1e|gq=b7f*1+1e$https://github.com/Mudassir-dev0ps/dotnetSampleApp","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792833753444}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1775":{"changeset":"Z:b8u>1|gq=b7f=1e*1|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834222281}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1776":{"changeset":"Z:b8v>1|gr=b8u*1|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834222852}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1777":{"changeset":"Z:b8w>o|gs=b8v*1+o$oct19jr-tfaodpPa$$w0rdR#","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834223416}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1778":{"changeset":"Z:b9k>1|gs=b8v=e*1+1$ ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834226325}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1779":{"changeset":"Z:b9l>1|gs=b8v=e-1*1+2$  ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834226911}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1780":{"changeset":"Z:b9m>9|gs=b8v=e-2*1+b$           ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792834227484}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1781":{"changeset":"Z:b9v>0|cy=8so-5|7=cc=l*1d+5$Part ","meta":{"author":"a.a2GFvzpczpf6O1dm","timestamp":1792836420117}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1782":{"changeset":"Z:b9v>0|cy=8so*1d+5|7=cc=l-5$Part ","meta":{"author":"a.a2GFvzpczpf6O1dm","timestamp":1792836422180}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1783":{"changeset":"Z:b9v>1|gs=b8v=z*9|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5","timestamp":1792841422237}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1784":{"changeset":"Z:b9w>2f|gt=b9v*9+2f$https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1uq54Xgiakpsv5MX7fTPL1ybvquvfhfoi?usp=drive_link","meta":{"author":"a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5","timestamp":1792841423101}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1785":{"changeset":"Z:bcb>1|gt=b9v=2f*9|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5","timestamp":1792841423819}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1786":{"changeset":"Z:bcc<30h|b8=85g|5g-2zh-10$","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792986368941}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1787":{"changeset":"Z:8bv<3f|bc=88e|1-10-2f$","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792986411556}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1788":{"changeset":"Z:88g>1|bc=88e*1+1$=","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987090441}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1789":{"changeset":"Z:88h>4|bc=88e=1*1+4$====","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987090996}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1790":{"changeset":"Z:88l>i|bc=88e=5*1+i$==================","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987091548}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1791":{"changeset":"Z:893>i|bc=88e=n*1+i$==================","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987092148}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1792":{"changeset":"Z:89l>h|bc=88e=15*1+h$=================","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987092611}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1793":{"changeset":"Z:8a2>b|bc=88e=1m*1+b$===========","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987093165}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1794":{"changeset":"Z:8ad>1|bc=88e=1x*1|1+1$\n","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987093962}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1795":{"changeset":"Z:8ae>1|bd=8ac*1+1$D","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987094547}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1796":{"changeset":"Z:8af>2|bd=8ac=1*1+2$ay","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987095108}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1797":{"changeset":"Z:8ah>1|bd=8ac=3*1+1$7","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987096140}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1798":{"changeset":"Z:8ai>1|bd=8ac=4*1+1$:","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987097142}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1799":{"changeset":"Z:8aj>1|bd=8ac=5*1+1$ ","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987097694}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1800":{"changeset":"Z:8ak>1|bd=8ac=6*1+1$2","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987098489,"pool":{"numToAttrib":{"0":["author","a.etherpad-system"],"1":["author","a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD"],"2":["heading","h3"],"3":["insertorder","first"],"4":["list","bullet1"],"5":["lmkr","1"],"6":["list","indent1"],"7":["list","indent3"],"8":["start","1"],"9":["author","a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5"],"10":["author","a.oIZ496sC0MvFJBbg"],"11":["list","indent2"],"12":["author","a.6fEK8VUdbD4cP299"],"13":["author","a.W8SlWkw9QzdnoaRT"],"14":["heading","h2"],"15":["list","indent4"],"16":["list","indent10"],"17":["list","indent9"],"18":["list","indent8"],"19":["list","indent7"],"20":["list","indent6"],"21":["author","a.v1tf3cnZGGlguTDX"],"22":["author","a.xz6wKKS5j76kPjlD"],"23":["author","a.rS0d1d8BEKDUrt1E"],"24":["heading","h4"],"25":["author","a.aMGFTUQcz8IEZ3mm"],"26":["author","a.Fln8zZWwNdatIBJx"],"27":["author","a.4UVIp0q8OaxadHwV"],"28":["list","indent16"],"29":["bold","true"],"30":["heading","h1"],"31":["list","number1"],"32":["list","bullet2"],"33":["start","2"],"34":["start","3"],"35":["start","4"],"36":["start","5"],"37":["start","6"],"38":["start","8"],"39":["start","9"],"40":["start","11"],"41":["start","12"],"42":["start","13"],"43":["start","14"],"44":["start","15"],"45":["start","16"],"46":["start","17"],"47":["start","19"],"48":["start","7"],"49":["author","a.a2GFvzpczpf6O1dm"]},"attribToNum":{"author,a.etherpad-system":0,"author,a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD":1,"heading,h3":2,"insertorder,first":3,"list,bullet1":4,"lmkr,1":5,"list,indent1":6,"list,indent3":7,"start,1":8,"author,a.XBtqZgC04nCR1sC5":9,"author,a.oIZ496sC0MvFJBbg":10,"list,indent2":11,"author,a.6fEK8VUdbD4cP299":12,"author,a.W8SlWkw9QzdnoaRT":13,"heading,h2":14,"list,indent4":15,"list,indent10":16,"list,indent9":17,"list,indent8":18,"list,indent7":19,"list,indent6":20,"author,a.v1tf3cnZGGlguTDX":21,"author,a.xz6wKKS5j76kPjlD":22,"author,a.rS0d1d8BEKDUrt1E":23,"heading,h4":24,"author,a.aMGFTUQcz8IEZ3mm":25,"author,a.Fln8zZWwNdatIBJx":26,"author,a.4UVIp0q8OaxadHwV":27,"list,indent16":28,"bold,true":29,"heading,h1":30,"list,number1":31,"list,bullet2":32,"start,2":33,"start,3":34,"start,4":35,"start,5":36,"start,6":37,"start,8":38,"start,9":39,"start,11":40,"start,12":41,"start,13":42,"start,14":43,"start,15":44,"start,16":45,"start,17":46,"start,19":47,"start,7":48,"author,a.a2GFvzpczpf6O1dm":49},"nextNum":50},"atext":{"text":"*Welcome for the training on Techno functional training program\nAgenda:\n  1.  Introduction\n  2.   LET  portal \n  3.   Day schedule (9 30am to 6 30pm)\n*    11 30  (20 minutes)\n* Lunch 1 30 ( 60 minute)\n*4  (20 minute)\n*\n   4. Lab guidance\n   5. Courseware\n   6. TOC\n   \n   9664670840\n   \n*   https://linuxlab.koenig-solutions.com\n*   Pa$$w0rd\n==================================================================================================\nApllication development:\n    Monolithic: \n    Microservice:\n        \n        components:\n            1)frontend ==>dotnet==>EFcore\n\n=================================\nSQL server==>DB server\n\nSSMS ==>Db client\n\nCRUD operation\n\nblameless postmortum\n\ncode===>build===>test==>deploy===>maintain\n==========================================\nAccount required for training:\n    ------------------------------------\ngithub\ndocker hub\nredhat\n==========================================\nDatabase\nUI\n\nDTO===>ORM\n=============================================\n*Day 2: 20/10/20\n\n\nhttps://github.com/Mudassir-dev0ps/dotnetSampleApp\n\nMVC\n============================================================\nusing Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;\nusing OrderManagement.Models;\n \nnamespace OrderManagement.Data\n{\n    public class ApplicationDbContext : DbContext\n    {\n        public ApplicationDbContext(\n            DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options)\n            : base(options)\n        {\n        }\n \n        public DbSet<Customer> Customers { get; set; }\n \n        public DbSet<Order> Orders { get; set; }\n    }\n}\n\n\n=\ndll===> format===>published application\n=========================================\nvar builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);\n \nvar app = builder.Build();\n \napp.MapGet(\"/\", () =>\n    \"Hello! My .NET application is running.\");\n \napp.MapGet(\"/about\", () => new\n{\n    Application = \"BuildPublishDemo\",\n    Technology = \"ASP.NET Core\",\n    Status = \"Running\"\n});\n \napp.MapGet(\"/health\", () => new\n{\n    Status = \"Healthy\",\n    Time = DateTime.UtcNow\n});\n \napp.Run();\n\n============================================================================\n*Day 3: 21/10/23\n\nDay 6 – Windows Server Fundamentals\n•\nWindows Server architecture\n•\nWindows Server editions\n•\nSystem configuration\n•\nWindows Server roles\n•\nServer Manager\n•\nUsers and groups\n•\nLocal vs domain accounts\n•\nActive Directory overview\n•\nGroup concepts\n•\nUser management\n•\nHands-on user/group administration\n\n======================================================\nOS\ndependencies\nlibraries\nApp code\n===========================================\n\nIdentity management ===>Authentication=================>IAM\nAccess managennt====>Authorization\n\nAD=============>Windows\nLDAP===========>Linux\nEntra ID====>Azure\nIAM===>AWS\n============================================================\nThe participants will act as junior Windows Server administrators for a fictional company. They will configure a server, install roles, create users and groups, deploy Active Directory, and troubleshoot access and account-management issues.\n\n1 role==>UI\n1 role==powershell\n------------------------------------------\nlocal user\n2 local group\n------------------------------------------------------------\nAD\nlocal user\n2 local graoup\n------------------------------------\n===================================================================\n*Day 3 22/10/26\n*Windows Filesystem & Permissions\n•\nWindows filesystem\n•\nDrives and partitions\n•\nNTFS\n•\nFile and folder permissions\n•\nNTFS permissions\n•\nShare permissions\n•\nPermission inheritance\n•\nOwnership\n•\nAdministrative shares\n•\nDisk space troubleshooting\n=============================================\n3GB====10x3==1000\n3GiB===2x10=3072\n==========================\nFolder1==========>f1,f2===>content ===================>UI\nFolder2=========>f3,f4========>content===========>Powershell\n\n*Access:          Folder          FIles\n    Read                  \n    Write \n    Execute \n    \n    ACL====> access control list          \n    ACE   \n    \n    icacls (powershell command for ACL access)\n    https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/icacls#:~:text=A%20sequence%20of%20simple%20rights,%2D%20Read%20and%20execute%20access\n    \n    \n#icacls C:\\NTFSDemo\\Finance /grant \"FinanceLab:(OI)(CI)M\"\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    \n    Learning principle\n    1)simple to complex\n    2)real to imaginary\n    3)part to whole\n    \n    =====================================================\n    Ownership:\n    -------------------------\n    \n    \n    \n \n------------------------------------------------------------\nRDP\n  \n   run -> sysdm.cpl ->remote-> allow remote connection to this computer\n\n  RDP-  Enable-NetFirewallRule -DisplayGroup \"Remote Desktop\" |  Select-Object DisplayName, Enabled, Profile\n  \n  Add user to Remote Desktop User group in win22 VM\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\n    ================================\n    Network file sharing\n    \n    SMB\n\noct19jr-tfaodp\nPa$$w0rdR#    RDP-  Enable-NetFirewallRule -DisplayGroup \"Remote Desktop\" |  Select-Object DisplayName, Enabled, Profile\n    \n   --------------------------------------\n \nAdministrative shares:\n       \nC$     Access the C: drive remotely\n        \nD$       Access the D: drive remotely, if available\n        \nADMIN$   Access the Windows installation directory, usually  C:\\Windows\n=========================================================================================\n*Day5 23/10/26    \n    \n*Windows Processes & Services\n\nProcesses\nThreads Services\nService dependencies\nWindows Services console\nTask Manager\nResource Monitor\nCPU troubleshooting\nMemory troubleshooting\nService startup failures\nService recovery\n===========================================================\nProcess vs Program\n\nmultiprogramming vs multiprocessing\n\nwindows==>run===>dxdiag\n\nProcess & Parent Process ->\n Get-CimInstance Win32_Process | Select-Object Name, ProcessId, @{Name=\"ParentName\"; Expression={(Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \"ProcessId = $($_.ParentProcessId)\").Name}}, ParentProcessId | Format-Table -AutoSize\n\n\ntasklist /svc\n\n\nTypes of processes:\n    1)foreground: 80% resource\n    2)background: 20 % resource\n    ==============================================\n    Process vs. Daemons\n    Service==============>daemon\n    Restart/Reload\n    ---------------------------\n    100 request\n    True positive /False positive                                             True               False\nTriage \n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMultithreading demonstration\n-------------------\nimport threading, time\n\ndef task(n):\n    print(f\"Task {n} started\")\n    time.sleep(2)          # simulates waiting (API/DB call)\n    print(f\"Task {n} done\")\n\nstart = time.time()\nthreads = [threading.Thread(target=task, args=(i,)) for i in range(4)]\nfor t in threads: t.start()\nfor t in threads: t.join()\nprint(f\"Total: {time.time() - start:.1f}s\")   # ~2s, not 8s\n\n=====================================================\n\nMultiprocessing .\n\nimport multiprocessing, time\n\ndef burn_cpu(n):\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(30_000_000):\n        total += i * i\n    print(f\"Process {n} done\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":      # required on Windows\n    start = time.time()\n    procs = [multiprocessing.Process(target=burn_cpu, args=(i,)) for i in range(4)]\n    for p in procs: p.start()\n    for p in procs: p.join()\n    print(f\"Total: {time.time() - start:.1f}s\")\n\n============================================================\n\nPython Releases for Windows | Python.org\n\n 1 -   $url = \"https://www.python.org/ftp/python/3.14.2/python-3.14.2-amd64.exe\"            >> Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -OutFile \"$env:TEMP\\python-installer.exe\"  \n \n2 -   $pythonDir = \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Programs\\Python\\Python314\"\n$scriptsDir = \"$pythonDir\\Scripts\"\n\n$userPath = [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(\"Path\", \"User\")\n$entries = @($userPath -split ';' | Where-Object { $_ })\n\nforeach ($dir in @($pythonDir, $scriptsDir)) {\n    if ($entries -notcontains $dir) {\n        $entries += $dir\n    }\n}\n\n[Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(\n    \"Path\",\n    ($entries -join ';'),\n    \"User\"\n)\n\n$env:Path = \"$pythonDir;$scriptsDir;$env:Path\"\n====================\nevent=====>incident\n\nlogs===>low level\nevent========>high level\n\nLogs/event\nseverity/priority================>importance\nsource===================>who\n==============================================================\n*Command                                 Purpose\nGet-Process                                    Lists running processes\nGet-Service                                     Lists services\nGet-CimInstance Win32_Process    Retrieves process details\nGet-CimInstance Win32_Service    Retrieves service configuration and status\nGet-Counter                                         Reads performance counters\nGet-WinEvent                                        Reads Windows event logs\nStart-Service                                         Starts a service\nStop-Service                                       Stops a service\nRestart-Service                                   Restarts a service\nSet-Service                                          Changes supported service settings\nGet-Process -Id                                   Inspects a process by PID\n================================================================\n*Day 6: 24/10/26\nWindows Logs, IIS & Firewall\n\nEvent Viewer\nWindows event logs\nApplication logs\nSystem logs\nSecurity logs\nIIS fundamentals\nIIS architecture\nWebsites\nApplication pools\nIIS bindings\nIIS logs\nWindows Firewall\nInbound/outbound rules\n===================================================\n\n\n\n\n<configuration>\n  <system.webServer>\n    <handlers>\n      <add name=\"httpPlatformHandler\" path=\"*\" verb=\"*\"\n           modules=\"httpPlatformHandler\" resourceType=\"Unspecified\" />\n    </handlers>\n\n    <httpPlatform processPath=\"C:\\inetpub\\myproject\\venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\"\n                  arguments=\"-m waitress --port=%HTTP_PLATFORM_PORT% myproject.wsgi:application\"\n                  stdoutLogEnabled=\"true\"\n                  stdoutLogFile=\"C:\\inetpub\\myproject\\logs\\python.log\"\n                  startupTimeLimit=\"60\"\n                  requestTimeout=\"00:02:00\">\n      <environmentVariables>\n        <environmentVariable name=\"DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE\" value=\"myproject.settings\" />\n      </environmentVariables>\n    </httpPlatform>\n  </system.webServer>\n</configuration>\n==================================================================\n\n====================================================\nhttps://github.com/Mudassir-dev0ps/dotnetSampleApp\n\n=====================================================================\nDay7: 2\n\n","attribs":"*1*2*3*4*5*8+1*1|5+45*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+o*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+p*1*3*6*5+1*1|1+f*1*3*6*5+1*1|7+1x*a*3*6*5+1*1+f*a|1+q*a*3*6*5+1*a+b*1|2+2s*1+2*a+1*1|m+bo*1+6*9|1+1*1|6+35*1*2*3*5+1*1|p+fe*d|3+4*1|m+cq*1+a*d|2+2*1|1+25*1*2*3*5+1*1|u+b4*1+8*9|1+1*1|g+gt*1+a*d+1*1|7+5i*1*e*3*5+1*1|1+f*1*2*3*5+1*1|s+d4*1*3*6*5+1*1|b+ai*1+4*a|1+1*1|4+4a*a|1+5*a+4*1|3+1v*1+j*a|2+6*a+4*1|2+1x*1+t*a|c+7j*a+1f*9|1+1*a|1+1o*1|4+1w*1+7*l|1+1*a|1+1*m+e*1|1+1*1+a*a+4*n+2y*a|2+6*a+3*1|3+1s*1+2*a+1*1|7+7l*1*e*3*5+1*1+h*a|1+1*a+4*1|1+1*1*o*3*5+1*m+s*1|i+97*9|1+1*a|2+6y*p|2+2*p+d*a|3+3*1|a+a1*1+7*a|2+2*a+u*1|1+22*1+5*a+9*1|2+z*a|v+ns*1|2+1q*a|1+1*l+14*r|2+2*r+4l*q+1*r|k+c6*r+1a*1|5+1p*1+o*q|1+1*1|3+1l*1+t*q|1+1*1|1+1r*1*3*6*5+1*1*t+1b*1|d+ny*1*u*3*5+1*1|1+g*1*t+s*1|e+4x*1+m*a|1+1*1+1f*a|n+l7*a+g*1|7+6s*1+7*9|1+1|1+1"}}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1801":{"changeset":"Z:8al>1|bd=8ac=7*1+1$6","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987099087}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1802":{"changeset":"Z:8am>1|bd=8ac=8*1+1$/","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987099647}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1803":{"changeset":"Z:8an>2|bd=8ac=9*1+2$1-","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987100185}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1804":{"changeset":"Z:8ap<1|bd=8ac=a-1$","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","timestamp":1792987100744}},"pad:techofunction-week1:revs:1805":{"changeset":"Z:8ao>1|bd=8ac=a*1+1$0","meta":{"author":"a.5Bma3U0RGBis5RkD","tim